This case includes this tree's own <new>/<exception>, whose std::exception, bad_alloc and bad_array_new_length members, vftables (??_7), deleting destructors (??_G), what() and placement operators (??2/??3/??_U/??_V taking a void *) are inline functions the header defines, so cxx1 emits them in the object; cl takes the same classes from vcruntime and inlines or imports them, and emits its own helpers instead (??_H vector constructor iterator, ??_E/??_G for the case's classes, __empty_global_delete, the printf it inlines from its headers). A difference between the two libraries, not a mangling one: the names both emit agree, and exception(char const *const, int) is spelled QEBDH as cl has it. One access letter differs by necessity: bad_alloc(char const *const) is private in vcruntime (reached by a friend class, which this compiler does not take yet) and protected here, so its name is IEAA where cl's is AEAA.
